0,Music of the Lesser Antilles - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_the_Lesser_Antilles,"French Antillean Carnival in Paris French Creole music is most famously associated with Martinique and Guadeloupe, though the islands of Saint Lucia and Dominica are also home to French Antillean music. Creole music is characterized by the prominence of the quadrille dance, distinct from the French version and related to the Haitian mereng. The quadrille is a potent symbol of French Antillean ...",Lesser Antillean French Creole,Creole
1,Antillean Creole - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antillean_Creole,"Antillean Creole (also known as Lesser Antillean Creole, Kreyol, or Patois) is a creole language that is primarily spoken in the Lesser Antilles. Its grammar and vocabulary include elements of Indigenous languages, African languages, French, and English.",Lesser Antillean French Creole,Creole
