4,French Caribbean Music - Melodigging,https://www.melodigging.com/genre/french-caribbean-music,"• In Martinique and Guadeloupe, Afro-Creole drumming traditions such as gwo ka and bélé blended with European social dances (quadrille, polka, mazurka) to produce biguine. By the 1930s, biguine jazz bands popularized Antillean sounds in Paris, establishing a transatlantic audience for French Antillean music.",Lesser Antillean French Creole,Creole
